3. Keep AI providers behind independent interfaces.
4. Avoid unnecessary dependencies and large libraries.
5. Avoid blocking the main thread.
6. Use asynchronous operations for database and network tasks.
7. Use pagination or lazy lists for large food databases.
8. Avoid unnecessary recomposition in Jetpack Compose.
9. Handle application lifecycle correctly.
10. Do not introduce memory leaks.
11. Keep the APK reasonably small.
12. Use stable, compatible library versions.
13. Do not introduce unnecessary background services.

The application must remain usable without requiring a personal backend server or user account.

All ordinary calculations and core functionality must work locally.

